# Install as /usr/lib/sysusers.d/hyprforge-greet.conf, then:
#     systemd-sysusers
#
# A group, not a user. The greeter itself runs as greetd's own `greeter`
# account; what needs creating is a group that owns the exported theme,
# so the people who are allowed to restyle the login screen are a
# nameable set rather than "whoever got there first".
#
# Making the export directory world-writable instead would let any local
# account choose what the login screen says and which image it loads
# before anyone has authenticated. That is not a privilege boundary
# anybody should be relying on, but it is not one to hand away either.
g hyprforge -
